IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sga3-76f-76g`

-- Tests for sga3-76f-76g.l4 (ss 76F and 76G; lines 8937-9049 of inputs/CoA1967.txt). Every expected value is decided from the text before the run.

-- (4) a company is solvent if: there is no ground on which it could be found unable to pay its debts; if it is intended to commence winding up within 12 months, it will be able to pay its debts in full within 12 months after commencement, otherwise it will be able to pay its debts as they fall due during the 12 months; and the value of its assets is not less than its liabilities and will not become less after the payment.
-- Inputs in order: no ground; intended to wind up within 12 months; able to pay in full within 12 months of winding up; able to pay as they fall due in 12 months; assets not less than liabilities now; assets will not become less after.
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(4) the company is solvent` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (1) payments out of capital or profits: allowed only if the company is solvent; a payment outside (a), (b), (c) is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(1) the payment may be made out of the company's capital or profits` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A) expenses of the purchase are within the payment in (1)(a).
#ASSERT `s 76F(1A) the payment is within the payment referred to in subsection (1)(a)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(1A) the payment is within the payment referred to in subsection (1)(a)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2) where the company is not solvent, a purchase is not lawful / a release is not valid ("shall not be lawful", "void"): FALSE; otherwise not covered.
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(a) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company pursuant to the agreement is lawful` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(a) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company pursuant to the agreement is lawful` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(a) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company pursuant to the agreement is lawful` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(b) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company following the variation is lawful` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(b) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company following the variation is lawful` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(b) a purchase or acquisition of its own shares by the company following the variation is lawful` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(c) the purported release is valid` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(c) the purported release is valid` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76F(2)(c) the purported release is valid` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (3) the offence: a director or chief executive officer who approves or authorises the purchase or release knowing the company is not solvent.
-- Inputs in order: director; chief executive officer; approves or authorises; knows the company is not solvent.
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) the penalty: "a fine not exceeding $100,000 or imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years" ("or", not "or to both").
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST (`s 76F(3) penalty` OF 100000, 3, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 76F(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The prohibition derived from the offence (the bearer is named: every director or chief executive officer).
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 76F(3) a director or chief executive officer must not approve or authorise the purchase, acquisition or release knowing the company is not solvent` (Director "D One") AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "D One" DOES `s 76F(3) approve or authorise the purchase or acquisition of the company's own shares or the release of obligations, knowing that the company is not solvent` AT 4
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76F(3) a director or chief executive officer must not approve or authorise the purchase, acquisition or release knowing the company is not solvent` (Director "D One") AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 76G(2) "the total amount of the purchase price": the price paid plus the expenses (brokerage, commission and so on): 1,000 + 50 = 1,050.
#ASSERT `s 76G(2) the total amount of the purchase price` 1000 50 EQUALS 1050
#ASSERT `s 76G(2) the total amount of the purchase price` 1000 0 EQUALS 1000
-- (1) the company reduces its share capital and its profits by the parts paid out of each.
#ASSERT `s 76G(1) the amounts by which the company must reduce its share capital and its profits` TRUE 700 350 EQUALS JUST (`s 76G(1) reductions` OF 700, 350)
#ASSERT `s 76G(1) the amounts by which the company must reduce its share capital and its profits` FALSE 700 350 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 76G(1) the parts paid out of capital and out of profits make up the total amount of the purchase price` 1050 700 350
#ASSERT (NOT `s 76G(1) the parts paid out of capital and out of profits make up the total amount of the purchase price` 1050 700 349)
#ASSERT (NOT `s 76G(1) the parts paid out of capital and out of profits make up the total amount of the purchase price` 1050 701 350)
-- The duty has no time limit and no stated consequence, so no trace can show it breached (listed under "Rules with no breach path" in NOTES.md).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 76G(1) the company must reduce its share capital or its profits by the total amount of the purchase price` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte Ltd" DOES `s 76G(1) reduce the amount of its share capital or its profits, or both, by the total amount of the purchase price paid for the shares cancelled` AT 40
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 76G(1) the company must reduce its share capital or its profits by the total amount of the purchase price` "Acme Pte Ltd" AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)
